1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,512
My skin doesn't show the time. It shows a countdown to the exact second I finally tell the absolute truth.

2
00:00:07,812 --> 00:00:14,988
For twenty-four years, I kept the numbers frozen by telling polite little white lies to everyone in my life.

3
00:00:15,288 --> 00:00:22,608
Then my boyfriend Leo asked if I loved his art, and the timer suddenly started running twice as fast.

4
00:00:22,908 --> 00:00:30,108
I lied and said his paintings were brilliant. The numbers slammed to a dead stop, mocking my cowardice.

5
00:00:30,408 --> 00:00:37,680
Three hours left. That is all the honesty-debt I have left before my time completely runs out forever.

6
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:46,092
I rush to my mother's house, desperate to confess every hidden secret before the final terrifying second strikes.

7
00:00:46,392 --> 00:00:54,744
She opens the door, smiling warmly, holding a framed photograph of the terrible accident we both survived together.

8
00:00:55,044 --> 00:01:03,972
The timer flashes red. Five seconds left. I have to tell her the crash was entirely my fault.

9
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:12,504
The clock hits zero. But I am still standing. My mother’s arm begins to glow instead.

10
00:01:12,804 --> 00:01:20,388
She whispers, I lied to protect you. Now the debt is yours. Are you brave enough to check yours?
